---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';

const areas = ['Midtown', 'Westport', 'Crossroads', 'Brookside', 'Waldo', 'Raytown', 'Independence', 'North Kansas City'];
---

<Base
  title="About | Oakspur Tire & Wheel, Kansas City"
  description="Oakspur Tire & Wheel is a family-owned tire shop in Kansas City, open since 2009."
>
  <section class="wrap page-head">
    <h1>A family tire shop since 2009</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Dale Hartwick opened Oakspur in a two-bay garage with a used tire machine and a hand-painted
      sign. His daughter Renee runs the counter now. Dale still balances wheels most mornings.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap split split--wide-right">
      <h2>How we work</h2>
      <div>
        <p class="lede">
          Dale spent eleven years at a chain store, where the job was to sell four tires to
          everybody who walked in. He wanted a shop where you could say "you've got another year on
          these" and mean it.
        </p>
        <p>
          That's still the rule. We measure your tread where you can see the gauge. We write the
          depth on used tires in yellow crayon so you know what you're buying. We post our prices
          and we stick to them.
        </p>
        <p>
          Today the shop has four bays and six people. Most of our customers were sent by a
          neighbor, a coworker or their mechanic.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--rubber">
    <div class="wrap">
      <ul class="numbers">
        <li>
          <span class="crayon">4</span>
          service bays
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="crayon">6</span>
          people on the crew
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="crayon">2009</span>
          the year we opened
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="crayon">30 min</span>
          for most flat repairs
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--paper">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2>Who we serve</h2>
        <p class="lede" style="margin-top:1rem">
          The shop is at {site.address.street}, a few minutes from downtown. Customers drive in from
          all over the metro.
        </p>
        <ul class="areas">
          {areas.map((a) => <li>{a}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>While you wait</h2>
        <ul class="ruled" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
          <li>
            <h3>A clean waiting room</h3>
            <p>Free coffee, Wi-Fi and a window into the bays so you can watch the work.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Early drop-off</h3>
            <p>Leave your keys in the drop box before work and we'll text you when it's done.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Fleet and work trucks</h3>
            <p>We keep a tab for local contractors and bill once a month.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .numbers {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 2rem 1.5rem;
  }

  .numbers li {
    color: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.85);
  }

  .numbers span {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.4rem);
    line-height: 1;
  }

  @media (min-width: 56rem) {
    .numbers {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .areas {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .areas li {
    padding: 0.35rem 0.8rem;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--rubber);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
</style>
